    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s, core %2$s</string>
    <string name="about_what_title">What it is</string>
    <string name="about_what_body">Phone navigator that keeps going when GPS drops.</string>
    <string name="about_outage_title">Lamps</string>
    <string name="about_outage_body">GNSS. Assisted. Dead reckoning. Reacquiring. Low confidence.</string>
    <string name="about_demo_title">How to demo</string>
    <string name="about_demo_1">Allow location.</string>
    <string name="about_demo_2">Wait for GNSS.</string>
    <string name="about_demo_3">Move a little.</string>
    <string name="about_demo_4">Long-press the lamp.</string>
    <string name="about_demo_5">The puck should keep moving. The halo should grow. The lamp should say Dead reckoning.</string>
    <string name="about_emulator">On an emulator, GPS and motion are fake.</string>
    <string name="about_no_obd">No OBD-II.</string>
    <string name="about_lab_title">Lab</string>
    <string name="about_not_title">What it is not</string>
    <string name="about_not_body">Not a laptop product. TimesFM is not on the phone. No OBD-II. No vehicle computer. No lane-level claim. Not certified for safety-of-life. Emulator shots use mock GPS and a fake IMU. They are not phone accuracy.</string>
    <string name="about_ai_title">AI on the phone</string>
    <string name="about_ai_body">A linear speed student on causal IMU features. It writes a pseudo-measurement. It does not overwrite position. TimesFM is not on the phone.</string>
    <string name="about_screening_title">Screening</string>
    <string name="about_screening_body">Held-out persist drift p50 is 0.5168 on 35 intervals. Official gate 0.10 is not met on IO-VNBD. kotlin_eskf_v5 leak-free: drift p50 0.611, endpoint p50 187.5 m, 1 Hz 0.257. Do not cite leaky-frame 0.541 as the headline.</string>
    <string name="about_notices">Third-party notices</string>
    <string name="about_notices_body">DriftZero is a research prototype. It is not certified for autonomous control or safety-of-life navigation. IBM Plex fonts are SIL OFL 1.1. MapLibre is BSD 2-Clause. Street tiles are OpenFreeMap from OpenStreetMap (ODbL). Photon, Nominatim, and OSRM are hosted services. See NOTICE.md in the source tree.</string>
